Rate limiting means oru IP address specific time period-la evlo requests send panna mudiyum nu limit set pannradhu.

Example:
- Maximum requests: 5
- Time window: 1 minute
- 6th request: 429 Too Many Requests
Install:
npm install express-rate-limit


Create middleware/rateLimiter.js:
const rateLimit = require("express-rate-limit");

const apiLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 60 * 1000,
  limit: 5,
  message: {
    message: "Too many requests. Please try again later."
  },
  standardHeaders: "draft-8",
  legacyHeaders: false
});

module.exports = apiLimiter;


Explanation:
- windowMs — time window.
- limit — maximum allowed requests per window.
- 429 — too many requests response.
- standardHeaders — rate-limit information in response headers.
